{"text": "INTEROFFICE MEMORANDUM\n\n@\u00ae CONFIDENTIAL = ur\n\nApril 6, 1988\n\nSubject: Weekly Highlights\nProduct & Applied Technology R&D\n\nTo: Dr. G. R. Di Marco -\n\nITEMS FOR WEEKLY BRIEF\n\nG7-1/G7-1 Implementation\n\nThe second stage of brands transitioned to G7-1/G7-2 is\napproximately 60% complete. Eight brand styles have been\ntransitioned with weight, size, and dilution on target and in\ncontrol. Minor problems have occurred when a brand experienced\ndifficulty with draft prior to the blend change.\n\nAccumulation of dust in Manufacturing has increased and a delay\nin the G7-1/G7-2 implementation is needed so that Engineering\nServices can develop a long-term strategy for dust storage;\ntherefore, brands which were scheduled to change May 2 will be\npostponed\u2019 one month or until June 1. When the Engineering\nServices costing study is complete in mid-April, Stage Iv will\nbegin.\n\nSidestream Smoke Measurements\n\nFinal nicotine analyses obtained with the BAT collection systen\nare in progress in support of ETS Division evaluation of\nalternative sidestream smoke measurements. A presentation to R&D\nstaff of the results of work with the BAT collection system will\nbe made the week of April 18. It is very likely that RIRT will\nuse the BAT collection system for future sidestrean studies.\n\nITEMS OF R&D INTEREST\nBurley Stem Extraction\nAnother lot of long K-stems have been rolled and cut with the\n\nHauni ATF cutter at Carolina Star Warehouse. Uncut stems mixed\nwith cut stems were produced; therefore, air classification will\n\nR.J.Reynolds Tobacco Cam nase\n\nBEST\nCOPY,\n\n\u20ac166 SpS0S",
